# Type Check Last

Type check is the final verification step. After it passes, stop and declare the task complete.

## Order of work

1. Implement the change
2. If UI/layout/behavior needs checking, do that **before** type check
3. Run type check last
4. Complete — do not start more verification

```text
❌ BAD
typecheck → open browser → click around → done

✅ GOOD
browser/UI check (if needed) → typecheck → done
```

## After type check

- Do **not** open the browser, take screenshots, or re-exercise the UI
- Do **not** start another verification pass “just to be sure”
- If type check fails, fix the types and re-run type check only
- If you still need a browser check, you ran steps out of order — do the UI check first next time, then type check again as the last step
